It seems like you are considering data here for just a single chromosome.  Depending on the length of the chromosome, there may be a reasonably good chance that the chromosome is inherited intact.

Regarding code, it seems like you're most of the way there but just need to identify the columns in gfreq that have their first value > 0.98 or < 0.02, which you'd then feed into the subset function (rather than hard-coding the -23, -25, -33, etc.)

Try this:

contaminants <- which(gfreq[1,] > 0.98 | gfreq[1,] < 0.98)
wxe10ril.sub <- subset(wxe10ril, ind= -contaminants)

karl

